New object literal created every render → new reference → child sees "changed" prop → re-render.

```jsx
// Bad: new object each render
<Child config={{ theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' }} />

// Fix 1: useMemo
const config = useMemo(() => ({ theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' }), []);
<Child config={config} />

// Fix 2: lift outside component (if static)
const CONFIG = { theme: 'dark', size: 'lg' };
function Parent() {
  return <Child config={CONFIG} />;
}

// Fix 3: memo on child
const Child = React.memo(({ config }) => { ... });
```

Root cause: JS object equality by reference, not value. `{} !== {}` always true.

Pick fix based on whether object depend on state/props. Static → lift out. Dynamic → `useMemo`. Child owns re-render logic → `React.memo`.
